Last year around this time I was called a gun-toting Nazi. And the
same "Xmas Spirit" (this is my guess) that is leading some to talk
about the horrors of capitalism and what it is doing to poor,
exploited people of color, happened last year. With the same effect.

Folks, this list is not very sympathetic--by charter and by history,
if not universally--to claims that what's wrong with libertarianism
and free markets is that it "hurts the poor." Or that J. Random Loser
did too many drugs and now can't get his shit together and can't get a
job and needs a bag of potatoes or somesuch (this was last year's sob
story).

I have no problem with posts questioning my premises, or even
disputing the logical conclusions I reach. But I deeply resent ad
hominem attacks--"gun-toting Nazi," "nerd," etc.--and I will continue
to fight back. 

Since the List rules disallow flaming (a rule only useful to those who
run crying to Harry, it turns out), but are now allowing the creation
of PPLs within the List, PPLs which can announce verdicts and
punishments, this allows a neat solution.

